    3. Mirror upper half vertically to get lower half; stack to form full object.
    4. Compute shift = boundary_row_width. Choose obj_col so obj_col + obj_width + shift <= 16.
       Choose obj_row so object fits vertically with margin.
    5. Place object on grid. This is the input.
    6. Output: clear object; color-swap both halves; place lower half at original position,
